  "description": "Learn words and phrases for talking about your body, sickness, and medical care.",
  "guidebook": "### Talking About Aches and Pains\nWhen expressing physical pain in Japanese, state the body part, add the subject particle **が (ga)**, and finish with **痛い (itai)**. For example, **頭が痛いです (atama ga itai desu)** means \"My head hurts.\"\n\n### Essential Health Phrases\n* **Taking medicine:** Japanese uses the verb **飲む (nomu)** meaning \"to drink\" for pills and medicine: **薬を飲む (kusuri o nomu)**.\n* **Catching a cold:** Use the fixed expression **風邪をひく (kaze o hiku)**. When you already caught one, say **風邪をひきました (kaze o hikimashita)**.\n* **Being tired:** Exhaustion is usually expressed in the past tense: **疲れました (tsukaremashita)**, literally \"I have become tired.\"",
